A body returns on the line of the end that closes it

The implicit return a block, a lambda or a method body closes with is given
the line of its closing `end` (or `}`), as CRuby's `leave` is. A body's last
line is then in its debug info, where the runtime reads it: a live_loop and a
with_fx flash their end lines, as native Sonic Pi's do (scheduler.rb
end_line_of, sp_host.c native_block_end_line). An endless method has no end,
and returns where it is. With a test in mrbc's bintest.

Made against the pinned commit in ~/Development/next-gen/mruby; applied to a
copy of the submodule by scripts/build-runtime.sh, never to the submodule.

diff --git a/mrbgems/mruby-bin-mrbc/bintest/mrbc.rb b/mrbgems/mruby-bin-mrbc/bintest/mrbc.rb
index 92994ef..1aa0677 100644
--- a/mrbgems/mruby-bin-mrbc/bintest/mrbc.rb
+++ b/mrbgems/mruby-bin-mrbc/bintest/mrbc.rb
@@ -261,3 +261,35 @@ assert('a super outside a method forwards no block') do
   assert_include result, 'SUPER'
   assert_not_include result, 'GETUPVAR'
 end
+
+assert('a body returns on the line of the end that closes it') do
+  # The implicit return a block, a lambda or a method body closes with is the
+  # closing `end` (or `}`), as CRuby's `leave` is: the last line of a body is
+  # then in its debug info, where a tool reading a block's lines (where its
+  # code ends) finds it. An endless method has no end, and returns where it is.
+  Dir.mktmpdir do |dir|
+    src = File.join(dir, 'ends.rb')
+    File.write(src, <<~RUBY)
+      proc do
+        1
+
+      end
+      proc {
+        2
+      }
+      l = -> do
+        3
+      end
+      def m
+        4
+      end
+      def e = 5
+    RUBY
+    out = File.join(dir, 'out.mrb')
+    result, status = Open3.capture2e(*(cmd_list('mrbc') + ['-v', '-o', out, src]))
+    assert_equal 0, status.exitstatus, result
+    # each irep's RETURN, by its line; the program's own first, then its bodies in order
+    returns = result.lines.grep(/\sRETURN\s/).map { |l| l[/\A\s*(\d+)/, 1].to_i }
+    assert_equal [4, 7, 10, 13, 14], returns.drop(1)
+  end
+end
